---
description: Go runtime standards for ClawdBot (github.com/8bitlabs/clawdbot). Apply when editing cmd/, pkg/, ooda/, web/, or zero-service.
globs:
  - "**/*.go"
  - "**/go.mod"
  - "**/Makefile"
  - "**/zero-service/**"
alwaysApply: false
---

go-runtime:

- Target Go 1.26.4+ (`go.mod`). Older 1.26 toolchains fail `govulncheck`.
- Keep changes small and package-scoped. Prefer `pkg/` libraries over growing `cmd/` binaries.
- Trading and funding paths stay dry-run by default. Live transfer or trade needs explicit opt-in and bounded limits.
- Never commit `.env`, wallet keypairs, install ledgers, or generated runtime state.
- Verify with `make test` and `make release-check` before claiming a change is shippable.
- Public surfaces: runtime `https://github.com/Solizardking/clawdbot-go`, hub `https://github.com/solizardking/solana-clawd`, gateway `https://zk.x402.wtf`, terminal `https://cheshireterminal.ai`.
